Null}(D))$, we reduce $D$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -7 & 9 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-5){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ -3 & 6 & -1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix has $3$ pivot columns and no non-pivot columns. \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\text{nullity}(D)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Null}(D))=0.\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186124883 1068 #edb/ref 17592186121868 13194139533420 17592186045585 false] [17592186124883 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320371 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186124883 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186124883 1071 "Consider the matrices given below. Find $\\text{dim(Null}(A))+\\text{dim(Null}(B))+\\text{dim(Null}(C)).$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186124883 1071 "Consider the matrices given below. Find $dim(Null(A)) + dim(Null(B)) + dim(Null(C))$.\n\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -4 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 false] [17592186124883 1074 "The dimension of the null space of a matrix is the number of non-pivot columns in the matrix. \n\nAlso, all of the given matrices are in row echelon form.\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each of the statements.\n\n- The matrix $A$ has $2$ pivot columns and 