\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{1}(4{x}^{3}+{t}^{5})\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}4{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{1}{t}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={x}^{4}{|}_{-1}^{1}+{t}^{5}x{|}_{-1}^{1} \\\\  & =(1-1)+({t}^{5}-(-{t}^{5})) \\\\  & =2{t}^{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{I}^{′}(t)=10{t}^{4}(2{t}^{5})=20{t}^{9}.\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320728 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320485 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320728 1069 "q-350585" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320728 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320728 1071 "Find the sum of the following series. Do not round the answer.\n\n$1+\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{1}{81}+⋯+\\frac{1}{{9}^{n}}+⋯=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320728 1072 #uuid "e7298c72-c366-5a91-8355-19f9ef267822" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320728 1074 "The first thing we notice is that we can rewrite the terms of the series as powers of $\\frac{1}{9}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1+\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{1}{81}+⋯+\\frac{1}{{9}^{n}}+⋯ & =1+\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{1}{{9}^{2}}+⋯+\\frac{1}{{9}^{n}}+⋯ \\\\  & =1+\\frac{1}{9}+{(\\frac{1}{9})}^{2}+⋯+{(\\frac{1}{9})}^{n}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we recognize that the series looks similar to the Maclaurin expansion for $f(x)=\\frac{1}{1-x}.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{1-x} & =1+x+{x}^{2}+{x}^{3}+⋯+{x}^{n}+⋯\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{1}{9}$ into our Maclaurin expansion gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{(1-\\frac{1}{9})} & =1+\\frac{1}{9}+{(\\frac{1}{9})}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{9})}^{3}+⋯+{(\\frac{1}{9})}^{n}+⋯ \\\\ \\frac{9}{8} & =1+\\frac{1}{9}+\\frac{1}{81}+\\frac{1}{729}+⋯+\\frac{1}{{9}^{n}}+⋯\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the series is $\\frac{9}{8}.$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320729 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320417 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320729 1069 "q-350591" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true]