)(x+5)}=\\frac{A}{x+4}+\\frac{B}{x+5}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x+4)(x+5)$ gives\n\n$$\n3x+10=A(x+5)+B(x+4).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-4$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-4)+10 & =A(-4+5)+B(-4+4) \\\\ -2 & =A \\\\ A & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=-5,$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(-5)+10 & =A(-5+5)+B(-5+4) \\\\ -5 & =-B \\\\ B & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3x+10}{(x+4)(x+5)}=\\frac{-2}{x+4}+\\frac{5}{x+5}.\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320764 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320668 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320764 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320690 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320764 1069 "q-350950" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320764 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320764 1071 "Express $\\frac{4x-1}{(x+1)(2x-3)}$ as a sum of partial fractions.\n\n| $\\frac{4x-1}{(x+1)(2x-3)}=\\,$ | {{field-1}} | $+$ | {{field-2}} |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $x+1$ |  | $2x-3$ |" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320764 1072 #uuid "6601da82-de98-5b52-8b98-1349b55ce4ef" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320764 1074 "Our task is to find $A$ and $B$ such that\n\n$$\n\\frac{4x-1}{(x+1)(2x-3)}=\\frac{A}{x+1}+\\frac{B}{2x-3}.\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides by $(x+1)(2x-3)$ gives\n\n$$\n4x-1=A(2x-3)+B(x+1).\n$$\n\nFor $x=-1$, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(-1)-1 & =A(2(-1)-3)+B(-1+1) \\\\ -5 & =-5A \\\\ A & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $x=\\frac{3}{2},$ we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(\\frac{3}{2})-1 & =A(2(\\frac{3}{2})-3)+B(\\frac{3}{2}+1) \\\\ 5 & =\\frac{5}{2}B \\\\ B & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{4x-1}{(x+1)(2x-3)}=\\frac{1}{x+1}+\\frac{2}{2x-3}.\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320765 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320208 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320765 1069 "q-350957" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320765 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533420 17592186045585 tru