5585 true] [17592186320766 1074 "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{1}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=4{x}^{5} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int 4{x}^{5}\\,dx=\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}4{x}^{5}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}u{v}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}v{u}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡x(\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{3}){|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}}-{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}(\\frac{2{x}^{6}}{3})(\\frac{1}{x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[\\frac{2({e}^{3})^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})}{3}-\\frac{2(1)^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)}{3}]-\\frac{2}{3}{\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}{x}^{5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{2{e}^{18}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{3})}{3}-\\frac{{x}^{6}}{9}{|}_{1}^{{e}^{3}} \\\\  & =2{e}^{18}-(\\frac{{e}^{18}}{9}-\\frac{1}{9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(18{e}^{18}-{e}^{18}+1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{9}(17{e}^{18}+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320767 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320653 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320767 1069 "q-350964" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320767 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320767 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{{e}^{3}}7{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320767 1072 #uuid "ef807bb7-47d6-5f52-9a90-8cae17c4e070" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320767 1074 "We will solve this problem using integration by parts. We start by defining $u$ and ${v}^{′},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}) & \\,⟹\\,{u}^{′}=\\frac{2}{x} \\\\ {v}^{′}=7{x}^{2} & \\,⟹\\,v=\\int 7{x}^{2}\\,dx=\\frac{7{x}^{3}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n