name{ln}⁡3\\cdot \\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $3$ | $81$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{81}\\frac{2}{x\\sqrt{{log}_{3}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2{\\int }_{3}^{81}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{log}_{3}⁡x}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =2{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3{\\int }_{1}^{4}{u}^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\cdot (2\\sqrt{u}){|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3(\\sqrt{4}-\\sqrt{1}) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{ln}⁡3(2-1) \\\\  & =(4)\\operatorname{ln}⁡3\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320820 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320615 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320820 1069 "q-351287" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320820 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320820 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{5}^{125}\\frac{8}{3x{log}_{5}⁡({x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x=($\n{{field-1}}\n$)\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡5$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320820 1072 #uuid "353ff421-65f8-59eb-b8ea-71a83d1ce946" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320820 1074 "Let $u={log}_{5}⁡({x}^{2}).$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\cdot 2x=\\frac{2}{x\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\,⟹\\,\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{2}\\cdot \\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nCalculating the limits for $u$ gives the following:\n\n| $x$ | $5$ | $125$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $2$ | $6$ |\n\nWe now substitute and evaluate as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5}^{125}\\frac{8}{3x{log}_{5}⁡({x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{8}{3}{\\int }_{5}^{125}\\frac{1}{{log}_{5}⁡({x}^{2})}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}x}{x} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{6}\\frac{1}{u}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{3}{\\int }_{2}^{6}\\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u|){|}_{2}^{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{3}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3 \\\\  & =(\\frac{4}{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡3)\\operatorname{ln}⁡5\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320821 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320678 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320821 1069 "q-351291" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320821 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320821 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{5-80{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320821 1072 #uuid "b439af01-6063-5a0d-8dfc-d235cf8c0346" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320821 1074 "Let's rewrite our integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{5-80{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =10{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5(1-16{x}^{2})}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{5}}{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-16{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(4x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nThis integral resembles the basic integral for inverse sine, \n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\text{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u+C.\n$$\n\nThe only difference is that instead of ${u}^{2}$ as the variable, we have ${(4x)}^{2}.$\n\nSo, let's substitute $u=4x.$ Differentiating, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nBefore substituting, we use the table below to change the limits from $x$ to $u.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{8}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $u$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nUsing the above, we can now write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{10}{\\sqrt{5-80{x}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1/8}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-(4x)^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{5}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{4}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1-{u}^{2}}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡u\\,{|}_{0}^{1/2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}(\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(\\frac{1}{2})-\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{2}(\\frac{\\pi }{6}-0) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi \\sqrt{5}}{12}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320822 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320532 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320822 1069 "q-351303" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320822 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320822 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{\\infty }\\frac{12}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320822 1072 #uuid "e24d3482-e9e4-5205-8528-f66c100fe517" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320822 1074 "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{\\infty }\\frac{12}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =12\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{a}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x\\,{|}_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{a} \\\\  & =12\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)-\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})) \\\\  & =12\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)-(-\\frac{\\pi }{3})) \\\\  & =12\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)+\\frac{\\pi }{3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, recall the end behavior of the function $y=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x,$ shown in the graph below:\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to -\\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$\n\n![](images/28/28afd0a065525cd225377165c2164a1ecc254b1be8aba60d64324d14430c3be4.png)\n\nUsing this to evaluate our integral, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{3}}^{\\infty }\\frac{12}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =12\\cdot ({lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)+\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =12\\cdot (\\frac{\\pi }{2}+\\frac{\\pi }{3}) \\\\  & =12\\cdot \\frac{5\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =10\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320823 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320416 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320823 1069 "q-351304" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320823 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320823 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}/3}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320823 1072 #uuid "26caa2b4-26f9-5ac4-bda8-58220bab9372" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320823 1074 "First, let's recall the following result:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x+C\n$$\n\nWe proceed by setting the upper bound equal to some parameter $a,$ integrating as usual, and then taking the limit as $a\\to \\infty .$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}/3}^{\\infty }\\frac{8}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =8\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }{\\int }_{\\sqrt{3}/3}^{a}\\frac{1}{1+{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }\\operatorname{arctan}⁡x\\,{|}_{\\sqrt{3}/3}^{a} \\\\  & =8\\cdot {lim}_{a\\to \\infty }(\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(a)-\\operatorn