17592186320914 1072 #uuid "45fc32fa-3c70-59c6-b5c6-1830a270fec5" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320914 1074 "The fourth-degree Taylor polynomial of $f(x)$ about $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{4}(x)= & \\,f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a)+\\frac{{f}^{″}(a)}{2!}(x-a)^{2}+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(a)}{3!}(x-a)^{3} \\\\  & \\,+\\frac{{f}^{(4)}(a)}{4!}(x-a)^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, we have $a=\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ so\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{4}(x)= & \\,f(\\frac{\\pi }{3})+{f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})+\\frac{{f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}{2!}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})}^{2} \\\\  & \\,+\\frac{{f}^{‴}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}{3!}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})}^{3}+\\frac{{f}^{(4)}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})}{4!}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we need to work out $f(\\frac{\\pi }{3}),$ ${f}^{′}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}),$ ${f}^{″}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}),$ ${f}^{‴}(\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ and ${f}^{(4)}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}),$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) & ⟹ &  & f\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )=-1 \\\\ {f}^{′}(x) & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{′}\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )=0 \\\\ {f}^{″}(x) & =-9\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{″}\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =-9\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )=9 \\\\ {f}^{‴}(x) & =27\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{‴}\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =27\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi )=0 \\\\ {f}^{(4)}(x) & =81\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) & ⟹ &  & {f}^{(4)}\\,(\\frac{\\pi }{3}) & =81\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi )=-81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${P}_{4}(x)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{4}(x) & =-1+0(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})+\\frac{9}{2!}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})}^{2}+0{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})}^{3}-\\frac{81}{4!}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})}^{4} \\\\  & =-1+\\frac{9}{2}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})}^{2}-\\frac{27}{8}{(x-\\frac{\\pi }{3})}^{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320915 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320391 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [1