\begin{aligned}\\int (x+1)^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)(\\frac{(x+1)^{3}}{3})-\\int (\\frac{(x+1)^{3}}{3})(\\frac{1}{x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+1)^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)}{3}-\\frac{1}{3}\\int (x+1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+1)^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)}{3}-\\frac{(x+1)^{3}}{9}+D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is an integral constant. \n\nSo, we get that the indefinite integral is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int 27(x+1)^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1))^{2}\\,\\text{d}x & =9(x+1)^{3}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1))}^{2}-18\\int (x+1)^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9(x+1)^{3}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1))}^{2}-18(\\frac{(x+1)^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)}{3}-\\frac{(x+1)^{3}}{9}+D) \\\\  & =9(x+1)^{3}{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1))}^{2}-6(x+1)^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+2(x+1)^{3}-18D \\\\  & =(x+1)^{3}(9{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1))}^{2}-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+2)+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=-18D.$\n\nFinally, we can work out the definite integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{e-1}27(x+1)^{2}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1))^{2}\\text{d}x & ={[(x+1)^{3}(9{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1))}^{2}-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+1)+2)]}_{0}^{e-1} \\\\  & =[{e}^{3}(9{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡e)}^{2}-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡e+2)]-[{1}^{3}(9{(\\operatorname{ln}⁡1)}^{2}-6\\operatorname{ln}⁡1+2)] \\\\  & =[{e}^{3}(9-6+2)]-2 \\\\  & =5{e}^{3}-2\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320954 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320692 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320954 1069 "q-352066" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320954 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320954 1071 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $(x-3)^{2}{y}^{′}=8$ that satisfies the condition $y(4)=1.$\n\n$y=\\,${{field-1}}" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320954 1072 #uuid "9bd28782-0820-5dae-86e8-4965e6266454" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320954 1074 "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{8}{(x-3)^{2}}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{8}{(x-3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =8\\int \\frac{1}{(x-3)^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8(-\\frac{1}{x-3})+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{8}{x-3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=-\\frac{8}{x-3}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(4)=1$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =-\\frac{8}{4-3}+C \\\\ 1 & =-8+C \\\\ C & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, our particular solution is\n\n$$\ny=-\\frac{8}{x-3}+9.\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320955 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320286 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320955 1069 "q-352068" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320955 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320955 1071 "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\sqrt{x+1}\\,{y}^{′}=4$ that satisfies the condition $y(3)=10.$\n\n$y=\\,${{field-1}}" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320955 1072 #uuid "c687828d-8060-5328-a166-293d79967235" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320955 1074 "First, we rearrange the equation to give\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=\\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x+1}}.\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate both sides with respect to $x,$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {y}^{′}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{x+1}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =4\\int (x+1)^{-1/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =4(2(x+1)^{1/2})+C \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{x+1}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo our general solution is $y=8\\sqrt{x+1}+C.$ To find a particular solution, we substitute the condition $y(3)=10$ into our solution and obtain a value for $C,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}10 & 