 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=10 \\\\ 5{x}_{2}=5 \\\\ -2{x}_{3}=-4 \\\\ 0=0,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the fourth equation, we get a true statement. Then, from the second and third equation, we get ${x}_{2}=1$ and  ${x}_{3}=2$ respectively. Substituting ${x}_{2}=1$ into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n3{x}_{1}+5(1)=10\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=\\frac{5}{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nFinally, ${x}_{1}=\\frac{5}{3}.$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320966 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320584 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320966 1069 "q-35217" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320966 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320966 1071 "Find the inverse of the function $f(x)=ax-7$, where $a$ is a non-zero constant." 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320966 1072 #uuid "abfc488e-a974-5dbc-b40c-2f281295336b" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320966 1074 "To find the inverse of a function, we follow these steps:\n\n**Step 1:** Replace $f(x)$ with $y$:\n\n$$\ny=ax-7\n$$\n\n**Step 2:** Swap $x$ and $y$:\n\n$$\nx=ay-7\n$$\n\n**Step 3:** Solve for $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =ay-7 \\\\ x+7 & =ay \\\\ \\frac{x+7}{a} & =y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Step 4:** Replace $y$ with ${f}^{-1}(x)$:\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\frac{x+7}{a}\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320967 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320174 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320967 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320561 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320967 1069 "q-352216" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320967 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320967 1071 "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{7x+4}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320967 1072 #uuid "6e65e0f7-2dfd-53b0-b88e-79422c957b77" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320967 1074 "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $7$ | $4$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-7$ |\n|  | $7$ | $-3$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{7x+4}{x+1}=7-\\frac{3}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{7x+4}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}(7-\\frac{3}{x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =7{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\text{d}x-3{\\int }_{0}^{2}\\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =7x\\,{|}_{0}^{2}-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|\\,{|}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & =7(2-0)-3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+1|) \\\\  & =14-3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡1) \\\\  & =14-3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,3\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320968 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320270 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320968 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320606 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320968 1069 "q-352219" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320968 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320968 1071 "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{8x+1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,23\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320968 1072 #uuid "c3103ae2-3b8e-5895-aa6b-7ed09ac750d9" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320968 1074 "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-3$ | $8$ | $1$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-24$ |\n|  | $8$ | $-23$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{8x+1}{x+3}=8-\\frac{23}{x+3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{8x+1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{2}^{4}(8-\\frac{23}{x+3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\text{d}x-23{\\int }_{2}^{4}\\frac{1}{x+3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =8x\\,{|}_{2}^{4}-23\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+3|\\,{|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =8(4-2)-23(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4+3|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2+3|) \\\\  & =16-23(\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡5) \\\\  & =16-23\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{7}{5}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320969 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320521 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320969 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320592 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320969 1069 "q-352220" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320969 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320969 1071 "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{9x+7}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,29\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320969 1072 #uuid "420b9f17-222f-5f30-947e-edc02435b92c" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320969 1074 "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $-4$ | $9$ | $7$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-36$ |\n|  | $9$ | $-29$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{9x+7}{x+4}=9-\\frac{29}{x+4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{9x+7}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{2}(9-\\frac{29}{x+4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\text{d}x-29{\\int }_{-1}^{2}\\frac{1}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =9x\\,{|}_{-1}^{2}-29\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|\\,{|}_{-1}^{2} \\\\  & =9(2-(-1))-29(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2+4|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|-1+4|) \\\\  & =27-29(\\operatorname{ln}⁡6-\\operatorname{ln}⁡3) \\\\  & =27-29\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{6}{3}) \\\\  & =27-29\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,2\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320970 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320337 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320970 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320508 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320970 1069 "q-352241" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320970 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320970 1071 "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{{x}^{2}+5x+3}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320970 1072 #uuid "0bdc239a-c197-5dcf-8032-23cf841953c6" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320970 1074 "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $1$ | $5$ | $3$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-1$ | $-4$ |\n|  | $1$ | $4$ | $-1$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+5x+3}{x+1}=x+4-\\frac{1}{x+1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{{x}^{2}+5x+3}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}(x+4-\\frac{1}{x+1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{4}x\\,\\text{d}x+4{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\frac{1}{x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{1}^{4}+4x\\,{|}_{1}^{4}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+1|\\,{|}_{1}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({4}^{2}-{1}^{2})+4(4-1)-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|4+1|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+1|) \\\\  & =\\frac{15}{2}+12-(\\operatorname{ln}⁡5-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{39}{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{5}{2}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320971 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320501 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320971 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320517 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320971 1069 "q-352246" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320971 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320971 1071 "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}+8x+7}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}} $-\\,9\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320971 1072 #uuid "3db4911c-3e88-55c4-b1e8-c1c8f669e9b4" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320971 1074 "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder. For this, we can use synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-4$ | $1$ | $8$ | $7$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-4$ | $-16$ |\n|  | $1$ | $4$ | $-9$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+8x+7}{x+4}=x+4-\\frac{9}{x+4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{{x}^{2}+8x+7}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}(x+4-\\frac{9}{x+4})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}x\\,\\text{d}x+4{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\text{d}x-9{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{1}{x+4}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{3}+4x\\,{|}_{0}^{3}-9\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+4|\\,{|}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}({3}^{2}-{0}^{2})+4(3-0)-9(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|3+4|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+4|) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}+12-9(\\operatorname{ln}⁡7-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4) \\\\  & =\\frac{33}{2}-9\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{7}{4}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320972 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320461 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320972 1069 "q-352247" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320972 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320972 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+5x-1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320972 1072 #uuid "42ce6d45-7dcd-53d8-be85-5db5b0c5d792" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320972 1074 "We first need to decompose the integrand into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe draw up a synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $3$ | $-7$ | $5$ | $-1$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $3$ | $-4$ | $1$ |\n|  | $3$ | $-4$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n\nSo from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+5x-1}{x-1}=3{x}^{2}-4x+1.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\frac{3{x}^{3}-7{x}^{2}+5x-1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{1}^{2}(3{x}^{2}-4x+1)\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-4{\\int }_{1}^{2}x\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}{|}_{1}^{2}-4\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}{|}_{1}^{2}+x{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}^{3}{|}_{1}^{2}-2{x}^{2}{|}_{1}^{2}+x{|}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =[{2}^{3}-{1}^{3}]-2[{2}^{2}-{1}^{2}]+[2-1] \\\\  & =7\\cdot 1-2(3)+1 \\\\  & =7-6+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320973 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320173 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320973 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320406 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320973 1069 "q-352248" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320973 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320973 1071 "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+3x+1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,\\,3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320973 1072 #uuid "206040ef-bb29-53ec-93de-6a7779eb0265" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320973 1074 "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-2$ | $1$ | $4$ | $3$ | $1$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-2$ | $-4$ | $2$ |\n|  | $1$ | $2$ | $-1$ | $3$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+3x+1}{x+2}={x}^{2}+2x-1+\\frac{3}{x+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}+3x+1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+2x-1+\\frac{3}{x+2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+2{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\text{d}x+3{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}{|}_{0}^{1}+{x}^{2}{|}_{0}^{1}-x{|}_{0}^{1}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}({1}^{3}-{0}^{3})+({1}^{2}-{0}^{2})-(1-0)+3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡|1+2|-\\operatorname{ln}⁡|0+2|) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+1-1+3(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{3}{2}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320974 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320535 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320974 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320542 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320974 1069 "q-352251" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320974 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320974 1071 "Evaluate the following integral:\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+2x+5}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x=$ \n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,\\,5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(${{field-2}}$)$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320974 1072 #uuid "d03569c5-c4ff-573e-985a-b2ccab879a81" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320974 1074 "The denominator of the integrand doesn't divide the numerator exactly, so we need to decompose it into its quotient and remainder parts, which we can do using synthetic division.\n\nWe start by drawing up our synthetic division table:\n\n|  | ${x}^{3}$ | ${x}^{2}$ | ${x}^{1}$ | ${x}^{0}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-2$ | $1$ | $3$ | $2$ | $5$ |\n|  | $↓$ | $-2$ | $-2$ | $0$ |\n|  | $1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $5$ |\n\nSo, from the synthetic division, we get that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+2x+5}{x+2}={x}^{2}+x+\\frac{5}{x+2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{{x}^{3}+3{x}^{2}+2x+5}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({x}^{2}+x+\\frac{5}{x+2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}x\\,\\text{d}x+5{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3}}{3}{|}_{0}^{1}+\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{1}+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{2}+5(\\operatorname{ln}⁡3-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{3}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{6}+5\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\,\\frac{3}{2}\\,).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320975 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320273 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320975 1069 "q-352284" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320975 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320975 1071 "Find the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ for $\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{3}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320975 1072 #uuid "63c14cb3-4078-51eb-8324-0b6413b29105" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320975 1074 "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{3}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}(3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\theta \\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}-\\frac{9}{8}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta )\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-\\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\frac{9}{8}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{2\\pi }{3})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{3})) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{9}{8}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{8}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\pi }{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320976 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320475 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320976 1069 "q-352303" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320976 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320976 1071 "Find the area $A$ bounded by the polar curve $r=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ for $-\\frac{\\pi }{4}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$A=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320976 1072 #uuid "9fccd036-7c2c-5e1b-84a8-5d35a0f5b2cc" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320976 1074 "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $, ${\\theta }_{1}=-\\frac{\\pi }{4}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{\\pi }{4}$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\