operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dx}{d\\theta } & =\\frac{5}{2}\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ) \\\\  & =5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into our formula for the second derivative, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{\\text{d}}^{2}y}{\\text{d}{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{\\frac{d}{d\\theta }(\\operatorname{tan}⁡(2\\theta ))}{5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{sec}^{2}⁡(2\\theta )}{5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\theta )} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{5}{sec}^{3}⁡(2\\theta ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320997 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320552 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320997 1069 "q-352520" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320997 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320997 1071 "The Taylor series for the function $f(x)$ about $x=0$ is given by \n\n$$\nf(x)={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}{x}^{n}}{(2n+1)!}.\n$$\n\nFind the series expansion of ${f}^{′}(x).$\n\n${f}^{′}(x)={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }$\n{{field-1}}\n$(-1)^{n+1}{x}^{n-1}$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320997 1072 #uuid "ba1a2065-05f5-5d7a-9aeb-6e943be02b88" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186320997 1074 "Writing the terms of the series explicitly, we have\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\frac{x}{6}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{120}+⋯+{{\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}{x}^{n}}{(2n+1)!}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{the }n\\text{th term}}+⋯.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above series term-by-term gives\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{2x}{120}+⋯+{{\\frac{(-1)^{n+1}n{x}^{n-1}}{(2n+1)!}}_{⏟}}_{\\text{the }n\\text{th term}}+⋯.\n$$\n\nWe can now write the Taylor series for ${f}^{′}(x)$ using the sigma notation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{n(-1)^{n+1}{x}^{n-1}}{(2n+1)!} \\\\  & ={\\sum }_{n=1}^{\\infty }\\frac{n}{(2n+1)!}(-1)^{n+1}{x}^{n-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [1