ue] [17592186321049 1069 "q-35283" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321049 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321049 1071 "Which of the following matrices have a rank of $6?$\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 5 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 7 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & 2 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 4 & 7 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321049 1072 #uuid "43599508-ddd2-50d6-b640-692e29bcfb0e" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321049 1074 "First, notice that a matrix of rank $6$ must have at least $6$ columns and at least $6$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the matrix $A$ since it has only $5$ columns and the matrix $B$ since it has only $4$ columns.\n\nAlso, the matrix must have $6$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $C$ has exactly $6$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(C)=6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$C$ only\"." 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321050 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320234 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321050 1069 "q-352848" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321050 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321050 1071 "Evaluate the following integral. Do not round the answer.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /6}\\frac{1-{tan}^{2}⁡x}{{cos}^{2}⁡x-{sin}^{2}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321050 1072 #uuid "af52ce4e-f719-5000-b6c3-23ef65c6c7c7" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321050 1074 "We use the identities $\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\operatorname{c