ula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=3{e}^{3t},\\,{y}^{′}(t)=2{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{2{e}^{t}}{3{e}^{3t}}=\\frac{2}{3}{e}^{-2t}.\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321122 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320450 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321122 1069 "q-353350" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321122 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321122 1071 "![](images/ab/abab926e465522d30b236577bf8a1654502807b864c9fed8a4cebb84efffd3a2.png)\n\nFor the parametric curve \n\n$$\nx=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,y=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0\\le t<2\\pi ,\n$$\n\nshown above, calculate the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve at the point where $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$ Do not round the answer.\n\n$m=$ \n{{field-1}}" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321122 1072 #uuid "88d2c31a-1162-5af9-962c-a704ed1fd8ff" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321122 1074 "We will use the formula\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{{y}^{′}(t)}{{x}^{′}(t)}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $x$ and $y,$ we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{y}^{′}(t)=-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t.\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{dy}{dx} & =\\frac{(-3\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}{2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, when $t=\\frac{\\pi }{4},$ the slope $m$ of the tangent to the curve is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m=\\frac{dy}{dx}\\,{|}_{t\\,=\\,\\pi /4} & =-\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}(1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321123 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320388 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321123 1069 "q-353351" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321123 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321123 10