heta +{e}^{\\theta }\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating at $\\theta =0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}(0) & ={e}^{0}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)+{e}^{0}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0) \\\\  & =1\\cdot 0+1\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{\\theta \\,=\\,0} & =\\frac{{y}^{′}(0)}{{x}^{′}(0)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321130 1068 #edb/ref 17592186320167 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321130 1069 "q-353418" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321130 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321130 1071 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=x+2,\\,y(-1)=0\n$$\n\nUse the Runge-Kutta (RK4) method with one step to approximate $y(0).$" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321130 1072 #uuid "98602b23-4a65-51ed-8d4a-761af9017b86" 13194139533420 17592186045585 true] [17592186321130 1074 "For an initial value problem\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=f(x,y),\\,y(a)=c,\n$$\n\nthe increment in $y$ using the Runge-Kutta Method with step size $Δx$ is computed as the weighted average of four sample slopes:\n\n$$\nΔy=\\frac{1}{6}({y}^{′}+2{y}_{1}^{′}+2{y}_{2}^{′}+{y}_{3}^{′})\\cdot Δx,\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n- ${y}^{′}=f(x,y)$ is the slope at the initial point $(x,y),$\n\n- ${y}_{1}^{′}=f({x}_{1},{y}_{1})$ is the slope at $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(x+\\frac{1}{2}Δx,\\,y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{′}\\cdot Δx),$\n\n- ${y}_{2}^{′}=f({x}_{2},{y}_{2})$ is the slope at $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(x+\\frac{1}{2}Δx,\\,y+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{1}^{′}\\cdot Δx),$\n\n- ${y}_{3}^{′}=f({x}_{3},{y}_{3})$ is the slope at $({x}_{3},{y}_{3})=(x+Δx,\\,y+{y}_{2}^{′}\\cdot Δx).$\n\nSince we want to find the value of $y$ at $x=0,$ we will use a step size of \n\n$$\nΔx=0-(-1)=1.\n$$\n\nFirst, we create a table and add the initial condition data.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,{y}_{1}^{′}\\,$ 